Desmond, Rosalind,<br />
<br />
The billing sample is finished and the custody question resolves the same w=
ay it did on the last one of these.<br />
<br />
Section 5(b) of Vandergrift Rowe's advisory agreement, in the version execu=
ted for 168 of the firm's 742 accounts, gives the adviser standing authorit=
y to instruct the client's custodian to debit advisory fees. The firm trans=
mits the debit file directly; the custodian executes without separate clien=
t authorization for each debit. Under Rule 206(4)-2 as amended effective Ma=
rch 12, 2010 that authority is custody of client funds. Item 9 of the firm'=
s Form ADV Part 1 answers "no" for both funds and securities.<br />
<br />
No surprise examination was obtained for calendar year 2010 and no independ=
ent public accountant has been engaged for 2011. No Form ADV-E has been fil=
ed. The 168 accounts hold approximately $141 million of the firm's $486 mil=
lion in regulatory assets under management.<br />
<br />
The rest of the draft is thin - a compliance manual that has not been revie=
wed annually since 2008, a code of ethics log missing two quarters, and a s=
olicitor agreement without the required disclosure statement. The custody i=
tem is the one that decides how this examination closes.<br />
